        <p>In board exams, short forms like <code>'d</code> require you to inspect the following verb:</p>
        <ul style="margin: 0.75rem 0 0.75rem 1.25rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: #cbd5e1;">
          <li><code>'d + V3</code> = <strong>had</strong> (e.g., <em>They'd met</em>)</li>
          <li><code>'d + better</code> = <strong>had</strong> (e.g., <em>You'd better go</em>)</li>
          <li><code>'d + rather / V1</code> = <strong>would</strong> (e.g., <em>He'd rather stay</em>)</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="example-box">
          They’d never met me before → <span class="highlight-tag">had they?</span>
        </div>
        <div class="example-box">
          You’d better not take a hard drink → <span class="highlight-tag">had you?</span>
        </div>
        <div class="example-box">
          She’d prefer tea → <span class="highlight-tag">wouldn’t she?</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Trap 2: Contractions 's -->
      <div class="card searchable">
